.TH "LMM" "1" "Nov 2026" "lmm 2.3.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
lmm-profile-finish - List and resolve a collection profile's items left to do


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlmm profile finish <profile> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Finish a profile imported from a collection.

.PP
A collection import installs every item it can. Each item it could not
install stays in the profile, in its place in the load order, as an item
left to do: why it is not installed, and what resolves it. With no flags,
this command lists them, with the command that resolves each. Deploy,
switch and apply still work on an unfinished collection, with a warning:
the game may not behave as the curator intended.

.PP
The actions (a mod is named by its id, or as source:id):
  --retry <mod>       try the install again; "all" retries every item. An
                      installer (FOMOD) that asks is answered at the
                      terminal, or with --fomod-choices / --fomod-defaults.
  --use-current <mod> a pinned file NexusMods no longer offers: install the
                      mod's current main file instead.
  --skip-file <mod>   a gone optional file: leave it out, install the rest.
  --skip <mod>        leave the mod out. The skip is recorded, so a
                      collection update does not add it back silently.
  --from <folder>     install the items you downloaded by hand from that
                      folder (as lmm profile fill does).

.PP
An archive an earlier attempt downloaded and kept is installed without
downloading it again. Each item resolves on its own: one that fails again
keeps its place on the list with the new reason.

.PP
Examples:
  lmm profile finish "Skyrim Plus" --game skyrim-se
  lmm profile finish "Skyrim Plus" --game skyrim-se --retry all
  lmm profile finish "Skyrim Plus" --game skyrim-se --retry 4044 --fomod-defaults
  lmm profile finish "Skyrim Plus" --game skyrim-se --use-current 266
  lmm profile finish "Skyrim Plus" --game skyrim-se --skip 999
  lmm profile finish "Skyrim Plus" --game skyrim-se --from ~/Downloads


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	print what the finish would do without changing anything

.PP
\fB--fomod-choices\fP=""
	answer FOMOD installer questions from a JSON file (the profile's fomod: shape or Vortex's choices array; key it by source:id when several mods ask, or by source:id#file-id for one file's installer)

.PP
\fB--fomod-defaults\fP[=false]
	answer FOMOD installer questions with the installer's own preselection

.PP
\fB--from\fP=""
	install the items downloaded by hand from this folder (lmm profile fill)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for finish

.PP
\fB--retry\fP=[]
	retry these items' install ("all" for every item)

.PP
\fB--skip\fP=[]
	leave these mods out of the profile (the skip is recorded)

.PP
\fB--skip-file\fP=[]
	leave these mods' gone optional files out and install the rest

.PP
\fB--use-current\fP=[]
	install these gone pins' mods at their current main file

.PP
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP[=false]
	auto-confirm installing from --from's folder


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	config directory (default: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lmm or ~/.config/lmm)

.PP
\fB--data\fP=""
	data directory (default: $XDG_DATA_HOME/lmm or ~/.local/share/lmm)

.PP
\fB-g\fP, \fB--game\fP=""
	game ID to operate on

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	output JSON instead of text; mutating commands print their result, --dry-run prints the plan; never prompts

.PP
\fB--log-level\fP="off"
	diagnostic log level written to stderr (off, error, warn, info, debug)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colored output (NO_COLOR env is also honored)

.PP
\fB--no-hooks\fP[=false]
	disable all hooks

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	verbose output


